00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:33.400
instructional tape, take them through that instructional tape a couple times so they

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.080
know how to execute every one of those techniques and they'll be aware of everything that they're

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:41.910
learning. Now what I want to do is take you through some of the basic fundamentals on what

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:45.790
to look for, what not to do, and what to do, okay? Now the first thing I want you to do

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.610
is when they throw in punches, make sure when they throw the punch, the elbow's never fully

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:53.700
extended like this, otherwise they're going to hurt the elbow and also the shoulders. Same

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.990
thing with the kicks. If they throw in a kick, make sure the leg is never fully extended. When

00:01:57.990 --> 00:01:59.490
and they get tired, they get a little bit of winded.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.580
Make sure they get some water, make sure they take a break, walking it out, catch their breath,

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:04.660
make sure they breathe properly.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:10.090
Just take the time and care with them and show them the love that they need to have by working out.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:13.890
And I truly believe if you get a young person up off the couch, you get them into working out,

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:17.830
it's going to change their life because that self-awareness is going to come into them even stronger.

